DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260306
SUMMARY:Lectio Terra: American Robin
DESCRIPTION:With Emily Dickinson\, Robert Ridgway.\n\nLast week were the fi
 rst morning bird songs that I have noticed\, riding quietly in the car wit
 h my partner after dropping our kids at school. I didn’t know it at the 
 time\, but that bright morning lay roughly equidistant between the final b
 lizzard of the winter (a nor’easter\, as they call it) and a season fina
 le of delicate snow turned into freezing rain. In this way\, the cold and 
 warmth\, dark and light\, liberations and rainy constraints of spring orga
 nize this month\, as we “interrupt” and “overflow” the patterns of
  winter yet linger in the “Certainty / And Sanctity” of our hibernatio
 ns. This…\n\nRead the essay: https://earthlyhours.com/lectio-terra/ameri
 can-robin/
URL:https://earthlyhours.com/lectio-terra/american-robin/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
