BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lt-0003-first@earthlyhours.com
DTSTAMP:20261112T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260312
SUMMARY:Lectio Terra: Sugar Maple
DESCRIPTION:With Annika Hansteen-Izora\, Walter H. Crockett\, E. Jones.\n\n
 Welcome to maple time\, if you live in my corner of North America. The sap
  of the sugar maple (Acer Saccharum) has been flowing now in most places f
 or several weeks\, and the sugar shacks are busy boiling off water to conc
 entrate sugar. Sap runs vary each year in timing and length based primaril
 y on temperature (freezing nights and warming days)\, though the sap’s s
 ugar content is affected by factors such as the previous summer’s weathe
 r. Like with the sap they carry\, sugar maple saplings wait to grow until 
 the circumstances are right\, and can persist in dense woods for long peri
 ods of time…\n\nRead the essay: https://earthlyhours.com/lectio-terra/su
 gar-maple/
URL:https://earthlyhours.com/lectio-terra/sugar-maple/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
