DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260320
SUMMARY:Lectio Terra: Paper Birch
DESCRIPTION:With Robert Frost\, Gifford Pinchot.\n\nPaper birch (Betula pap
 yrifera)\, also known as canoe birch or American white birch\, is a mid-si
 zed deciduous tree native to northern North America. It can be found acros
 s the northern half of the continent. Paper birch sap begins flowing near 
 the end of sugar maple season\, when daytime temperatures reach above 50 d
 egrees Fahrenheit\, and continues to run for only two to three weeks\, app
 roximately half as long as maple sap. Although black and yellow birch are 
 more commonly used to produce birch beer\, which pairs their sap with wint
 ergreen oils distilled from their bark\, paper birch is best for…\n\nRea
 d the essay: https://earthlyhours.com/lectio-terra/paper-birch/
URL:https://earthlyhours.com/lectio-terra/paper-birch/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
