DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260417
SUMMARY:Lectio Terra: Eastern Cottontail
DESCRIPTION:With Zora Neale Hurston\, Ernest Thompson Seton.\n\nFew creatur
 es are more storied than the rabbit and its cousin\, the hare. Their manif
 estations extend across the globe\, ranging from cosmology and folklore (N
 anabozho and Br’er Rabbit) into transatlantic children’s literature (L
 ewis Carroll’s “White Rabbit\,” Peter Rabbit\, and Peter Cottontail)
 \, and onward to twentieth-century cartoons (Bugs Bunny\, Roger Rabbit) an
 d cinematic riddles (the eponymous Harvey and Donnie Darko’s Frank)—le
 t’s not get into the other versions of bunnies in American pop culture. 
 Across their many forms\, these leporine figures embody a variety of trait
 s and entities…\n\nRead the essay: https://earthlyhours.com/lectio-terra
 /eastern-cottontail/
URL:https://earthlyhours.com/lectio-terra/eastern-cottontail/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
