DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260515
SUMMARY:Lectio Terra: Common Lilac
DESCRIPTION:With Amy Lowell\, Ronald Firbank.\n\nThe lilac—so pure\, so s
 weet\, so artificial. Although only 20 to 25 species of lilacs exist in th
 e wild\, more than 2\,000 named cultivars (according to the official Inter
 national Lilac Registrar) have been developed\, most over the past 150 yea
 rs. Beginning in the 1870s\, French botanists Victor and Marie Louise Lemo
 ine began using needles\, tweezers\, and paintbrushes to delicately cross 
 the common lilac—native to the Balkan Peninsula but common throughout Eu
 rope—with species from China and other regions\, creating spectacular do
 uble-flowered and early-blooming hybrids. Other breeders around the…\n\n
 Read the essay: https://earthlyhours.com/lectio-terra/common-lilac/
URL:https://earthlyhours.com/lectio-terra/common-lilac/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
