DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260612
SUMMARY:Lectio Terra: Pink Lady’s Slipper
DESCRIPTION:With Grace Greylock Niles\, C.S. Young.\n\nAlong the same walk 
 that I first encountered the wool sower wasp\, I found an old friend. No\,
  not that type of old friend—just a flower I’ve come to know over the 
 past nine or so years. It has a delicate yet visceral form\, immediately s
 triking and beautiful but a bit gory if you think about it for too long. I
 t’s the type of plant that seems to have nearly universal appeal\, spawn
 ing refined social and scientific clubs while also luring weirdos out into
  the woods. For independent botanist and artist Grace Greylock Niles\, who
 se work and story are worth knowing\, this flower took the front page of
 …\n\nRead the essay: https://earthlyhours.com/lectio-terra/pink-ladys-sl
 ipper/
URL:https://earthlyhours.com/lectio-terra/pink-ladys-slipper/
