UID:lt-0020-first@earthlyhours.com
DTSTAMP:20261112T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260719
SUMMARY:Lectio Terra: Corn
DESCRIPTION:With Haudenosaunee Storytellers\, Emily Pauline Johnson.\n\nIn 
 my personal opinion\, much resisted by the chatbots I consulted\, corn is 
 the berries of the vegetable world. Indeed\, corn—specifically\, sweet c
 orn—is unique among commonly eaten plants in that it spans the typically
  distinct categories of fruit\, vegetable\, and grain. In other words\, it
 ’s a grass that produces sweet clusters that you eat like a carrot. The 
 chatbots don’t know everything yet.\n\nRead the essay: https://earthlyho
 urs.com/lectio-terra/corn/
URL:https://earthlyhours.com/lectio-terra/corn/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
