BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lt-0029-first@earthlyhours.com
DTSTAMP:20261112T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260927
SUMMARY:Lectio Terra: Shagbark Hickory
DESCRIPTION:With Carl Sandburg\, Vladimir Nabokov\, Charles S. Sargent.\n\n
 Few trees in New England\, except perhaps the marvelous paper birch (Betul
 a papyrifera)\, have quite the visual appeal of the shagbark hickory. The 
 distinction is in the name. A fully shagged-out trunk embodies something b
 etween an elegant cascade and a strewn-out mess—a poise we might all hop
 e to achieve\, if we are so lucky.\n\nRead the essay: https://earthlyhours
 .com/lectio-terra/shagbark-hickory/
URL:https://earthlyhours.com/lectio-terra/shagbark-hickory/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
