DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261108
SUMMARY:Lectio Terra: Wintergreen
DESCRIPTION:With Jacob Bigelow\, Henry David Thoreau\, Linda M. Sweeting.\n
 \nInstead of receiving its first frost this week\, the Boston area experie
 nced a final illusion of summer\, with clear blue skies and gentle warm br
 eezes. Then the rain set in for a few days. The long-lasting summer has\, 
 paradoxically\, spurred some early reflections on winter. Though we haven
 ’t actually experienced any true cold yet\, I’m preparing my psyche fo
 r the insular dimensions of the impending change of season: cabin fever\, 
 layered attire\, dark afternoons\, and all the rest. My psychic preparatio
 ns are being aided by the example of the humble wintergreen plant\, which 
 has developed a form of…\n\nRead the essay: https://earthlyhours.com/lec
 tio-terra/wintergreen/
URL:https://earthlyhours.com/lectio-terra/wintergreen/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
